+/* _xeno_sound_adpcm: SPU-faithful streaming synthesis.                    */
+/*                                                                         */
+/* Replaces decode-at-keyon + OpenAL cubic pitch resampling with the SPU's */
+/* own pipeline, per psx-spx: integer-exact ADPCM block decode (five       */
+/* filters {0,60,115,98,122}/{0,0,-52,-55,-60} over /64 with (+32)>>6      */
+/* rounding, clamp16, shift 13-15 acts as 9), hardware loop flags          */
+/* (LoopStart latches the repeat address at block decode; LoopEnd jumps    */
+/* after the block completes; End+Mute additionally forces Release with    */
+/* envelope 0), and the SPU resampler: a 16-bit pitch counter stepped by   */
+/* VxPitch (clamped 4000h) whose bits 4-11 index the 512-entry Gaussian    */
+/* table for 4-tap interpolation (each product SAR 15, then summed).       */
+/* Output is fixed-rate 44100 mono PCM through AL_SOFT_callback_buffer     */
+/* with AL_PITCH pinned to 1.0; mid-note pitch changes are read live.      */
+/*                                                                         */
+/* CONCURRENCY (the load-bearing design): the callback runs on OpenAL's    */
+/* MIXER THREAD. All stream state (SPUALStream), the raw pitch/addr attrs  */
+/* it reads, and SPU-RAM writes are guarded by s_StreamMutex.  LOCK        */
+/* ORDER: g_SpuMutex may nest OUTSIDE s_StreamMutex (tick paths take       */
+/* g_SpuMutex then briefly s_StreamMutex); the callback takes ONLY         */
+/* s_StreamMutex; NO code calls into OpenAL while holding s_StreamMutex.   */
+/* This forbids the AL-internal-lock / stream-lock inversion, so the       */
+/* mixer can never deadlock against the 240Hz tick.  End+Mute crosses     */
+/* back to the tick via an atomic flag (SDL_AtomicSet/Get).                */
+/* ====================================================================== */
